  "2026-06-06T18:32:16.393Z",github-triage-subagent,"Dependency/security/CI triage 2026-06-06: gh pr list and gh issue list returned no open PRs/issues. Latest main Docs run 27070220668 and CI run 27070220656 both succeeded on 2026-06-06T18:21Z. Recent failed PR CI runs were superseded by later green reruns; latest inspected failures were run 27069299676 failing Gates (static) because CHANGELOG.md was out of date and run 27068207523 failing Gates (static) with one directory_load static-quality violation. Latest scheduled Auto Release run 27054598676 succeeded. Recommended CI/release action: no immediate fix; keep changelog:pm:check and static-quality gate as required pre-push checks on branches."
  "2026-06-09T23:16:51.499Z",codex-active-pm-cycle-20260610,"Active-cycle PR opened: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/192 on branch feat/active-cycle-settings-reindex-telemetry-changelog. AI review loop executed across pushes; only unresolved merge blocker is literal all-src coverage gate."
  "2026-07-21T15:56:06.972Z",codex-tracker-governance,"CI and continuous-improvement planning review 2026-07-21: the quality surface is already decomposed across pm-qwoy security findings, pm-gnzh Scorecard, pm-vlnc DeepSource, pm-92if CodeFactor and maintainability ratchets, pm-0yi7 fuzzing or property testing, coverage and contract gates, release health, telemetry, and exact-head scanner workflows. Future gates should remain contract-generated, warning-free, reproducible on clean installs, mutation-aware, and ratcheted so baselines can only improve. Scanner findings stay individually triageable pm issues; broad CI umbrellas must not hide per-finding ownership."
  "2026-07-21T16:07:17.090Z",codex-tracker-governance,"Exact-head CI evidence after direct-main tracker publication: commit 669055d9757850cdb54da198ab18df75312192d4 produced 22 green or neutral checks and one failing Gates (compat) job (run 29846552505, job 88688713860). Local and clean-published-version reproduction traced the failure to compatibility-check seeding reading only item.id after pm-nilh intentionally promoted top-level compact mutation IDs. Canonical regression pm-pkdpyz now owns the parser, regression tests, clean compatibility proof, and exact-head green acceptance gate."
  "2026-07-31T10:17:24.755Z","harness:codex","Release and CI organization 2026-07-31: daily schedule correctness, one-release-per-day keying, tag/changelog/registry reconciliation, and reliability SLO are separate defects with an explicit prerequisite chain. GA additionally waits for mutation quality, defect-escape ratchets, cross-version workspace compatibility, and exact published-tarball agent-session acceptance. Local and hosted gates should share the same contract fixtures and defect-derived regressions; a green single run is not reliability evidence, and package versions alone are not consumer proof."
  "2026-08-01T20:21:51.161Z","harness:codex","CI and release operating model 2026-08-01: local and hosted verification derive from one versioned gate registry and must prove parity. Every positive gate carries a negative control or mutation that it must reject; deterministic fault, concurrency, property, fuzz, security, cross-platform, contract, package-boundary, token-budget, and installed-consumer lanes cover distinct failure classes. Release state is a reconciled proof across source SHA and tree, generated changelog, immutable tag, GitHub artifact, npm metadata and tarball, direct install, npx, package-selected npx, Bun install, and bunx. Scheduled automation may produce at most one automatic UTC-day release when product changes exist; manual dispatch never moves a tag or disguises a failed schedule; tracker-only changes do not force empty product releases. Reliability is an SLO over event-partitioned runs and stage outcomes, not the latest green row."
  "2026-08-03T07:07:21.910Z","harness:codex","Dependency evidence 2026-08-03: Dependabot PR #877 upgraded CodeQL Action 4.37.3 to 4.37.4 and CodSpeed 4.18.5 to 5.0.1. Refreshed exact-head checks passed CI, literal coverage, Windows, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, static, docs, compatibility, and smoke gates; all bot comments were reacted to and individually acknowledged before squash merge bbbc13b58. Live Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning alert inventories were empty."
  "2026-08-03T08:23:10.144Z","harness:codex","Release-gate evidence for the broad SDK/CLI tranche: docs/type/static/duplicate/package-boundary/token/context/retrieval/coverage/version/secret/npx/package-dogfood gates passed; full coverage is 6,758 tests at 100/100/100/100. The final local release registry correctly stops only at greptile-review because the code is not committed yet. One governance import-cost sample transiently exceeded its bound on the first run; the exact isolated check and subsequent registry run passed all 10 entrypoints."
  "2026-08-03T08:54:50.210Z","harness:codex","Fresh GitHub/release inventory 2026-08-03 for the broad SDK/CLI tranche: zero open PRs; every one of 26 open issues has a comment containing its canonical pm-item link; Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning each report zero open alerts; pnpm audit is clean. The only outdated dependencies are the two incompatible majors already owned by pm-ksr40d and pm-do5b. Auto Release run 30788639874 succeeded as a tracker-only no-op after detecting one tracker-only commit since v2026.8.3, emitted no new tag, and the repository still has exactly one 2026-08-03 release."
  "2026-08-03T11:15:50.561Z","harness:codex","CI and release organization 2026-08-03: capability completion is explicitly blocked by scheduled reliability measurement, documented schedule behavior, exact published-artifact acceptance, and history-derived recurrence protection. Individual historical regressions remain linked through pm-1qkivy rather than duplicated as new generic CI chores."
notes[2]:
  - created_at: "2026-07-25T06:22:46.687Z"
    author: "harness:claude-code"
    text: "CI severity doctrine, drafted 2026-07-25. The standing requirement is that the pipeline should surface any defect that could reach a user, and the honest way to hold that requirement is to state what class of defect each gate can and cannot catch, then fill the gaps deliberately.\n\nWhat is gated today: correctness on the happy and error paths (full suite, 100 percent literal coverage), static quality and complexity ceilings, type checking, contract drift, lint and duplication, SDK import boundary, secret scanning, dependency and code scanning across four external analyzers, changelog drift, version lockstep, scale latency and memory at 10k, benchmark comparison per PR, and a mandatory exact-head zero-new-issues analyzer gate at release.\n\nWhat that set structurally cannot catch, with the owning item for each:\n- Tests that pass while asserting nothing meaningful. Coverage measures execution, not detection. Owner: mutation-testing gate (pm-zclzll).\n- Defects that escaped once and can escape again the same way. Owner: defect-escape ratchet (pm-rtn5h6).\n- Races, partial writes, and crash-interleaving faults, which are invisible to a deterministic suite. Owner: fault and concurrency simulation (pm-a8lnoh), with the three known open races as its acceptance targets.\n- Divergence between branches and between releases: multi-branch merge conformance (pm-76dnfg) and cross-version workspace compatibility (pm-pae3wo).\n- Nondeterminism that erodes the meaning of a red build. Owner: flake detection and quarantine ratchet (pm-zlv8jl).\n- Documentation that is wrong in a way no test executes. Owner: executable documentation gate (pm-xgcp18).\n- Public API breakage for downstream packages, which no internal test can see. Owner: SDK surface snapshot and breaking-change gate (pm-e6tm5c).\n- Surface regrowth that quietly undoes the grammar consolidation. Owner: command-grammar conformance gate (pm-wt43zj).\n- Agent-experience regressions - more tokens or more turns for the same task - which every functional gate is blind to. Owner: golden transcript replay (pm-8pnj).\n- Retrieval quality regressions, the only hot path with no quality measurement at all. Owner: retrieval quality contract (pm-p1g43q).\n\nTwo policies that keep the set honest. First, a gate is only worth adding if it can fail: any check that has never failed and cannot be made to fail on a deliberately broken input is decoration, and each new gate should ship with the negative test that proves it bites. Second, every escaped defect closes with a gate, not only with a fix - that is the ratchet, and it is the mechanism by which this list is expected to keep growing without anyone brainstorming it again."
  - created_at: "2026-07-29T21:26:15.719Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "CI, delivery, and release control model\n\nLocal fast gates: build and typecheck, lint/static architecture, focused unit tests, documentation and contract generation checks, token-surface budgets, and changed-surface package smoke. Pre-merge gates add literal all-source 100 percent coverage, mutation-score ratchets, property and fuzz suites, concurrency simulation seeds, storage/history drift validation, merge-driver conformance, cross-version matrices, security scanning, package-boundary and SDK-parity checks, and negative controls proving each gate can fail.\n\nHosted gates repeat deterministic controls on supported OS/runtime matrices and add CodeQL, dependency/supply-chain analysis, scorecard, performance regression, external package fleet smoke, clean packed-consumer installs, and immutable artifact provenance. Any escaped defect adds a reproducer and a gate under pm-rtn5h6; flaky tests are quarantined only with an item and a shrinking budget, never rerun until green.\n\nRelease semantics: scheduled automation publishes only when immutable product changes exist since the last tag; one UTC-day auto-release maximum; a manual dispatch may verify or request a deliberate release but never moves an existing tag; preparation is idempotent; npm and GitHub artifacts are compared by immutable version/tree/digest; fresh isolated consumers test direct install, npx, package-selected npx, bun install, and bunx using real dispatch plus a failing negative control. Tracker-only commits remain attributable without forcing an empty product release."
    edited_at: "2026-07-29T21:28:01.520Z"
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T12:41:53.007Z","harness:claude-code","A gate that has silently stopped detecting its failure mode is strictly worse than no gate, because it converts every subsequent green run into false confidence, and nothing in a normal pipeline can distinguish the two states. The only mechanism that detects gate erosion is a negative control — a deliberately broken input the gate must reject, run as part of the pipeline. This generalizes past CI: every assertion this project makes about itself, including validation checks, conformance gates, and property suites, should be paired with an input it must fail on, or it is unverified."
body: "## Charter\nLiving capability epic for docs, onboarding, release, and CI health: docs/ tree accuracy, docs-skills-gate link validation, CHANGELOG generation (pm-changelog), daily date-based auto-release, CI Gates (static + coverage + windows-regression + nightly), and contributor onboarding.\n\n## Scope\n- In: docs freshness gates, changelog:pm:check drift gate, auto-release workflow (RELEASE_PAT, Sentry gate), nightly matrix failures, coverage gate (100% literal all-src per ADR pm-w13j).\n- Out: telemetry/Sentry runtime behavior (pm-5oj5), code-quality ratchets (pm-92if).\n\n## Standing invariants\n- CHANGELOG is fully auto-generated from CLOSED items; regen is the LAST step of any change (updated_at bucketing trap).\n- NEVER change package.json version manually; releases are date-based (2026.<month>.<day>) cut by the daily workflow.\n- windows-regression job is the oracle for Windows path/shebang issues.\n\n## Open children (2026-07-04)\n- pm-7zs0 — recurring reminder: verify daily auto-release tagged AND advanced npm latest.\n- pm-lt6n — GH-427 Windows Node 24 nightly: POSIX-only error-code assertions (in progress).\n- pm-esbt — docs-skills-gate: validate anchor fragments in relative links."
